Hello everyone! Introducing the March 25 update and what's going to change in the game:

Game Economy

—"Packs of Perfection" and "Sealing Wax Packs" promos have been added. 

What’s New

— Starting slot number for all new characters in the “Equipment”, “Consumables”, “Trophies” and “Craft” tabs has been increased from 17 to 36 cells. The change does not affect the number of slots on already created characters (their number of slots remains unchanged). If your current character has less than 36 slots in the corresponding inventory tab and you have created a new character with expanded slots, the missing slots will be discounted for previously created characters.
— Automatic detection of game language at the first launch in Steam has been added. The game language now depends on Steam interface language;
— First phase of party matchmaking mechanics has been added.

How it works?

1.	The matchmaking works within the party leader's location based on the difference in character levels;
2.	Initially, players with a difference of up to 5 levels are being searched for, with time this difference increases to a maximum of 25 levels;
3.	If the party leader moves to a new location, the matchmaking continues there.
4.	Parties are merged automatically;
5.	The leader of the biggest party will become the leader of the common one;
6.	Matchmaking disables when the party reaches 8 players or when the leader turns it off;
7.	The leader can turn on matchmaking if there are less than 8 players in the party;
8.	The search icon will be visible only to the party leader with new players joining immediately.

Stay tuned for more matchmaking mechanics updates and improvements!

Huge thanks to External Testing Academy for helping us making the game better every day!

Game Economy


— The "Northern Defenders Pack" promo is now available;
— Players that received Community Ban on Steam, unfortunately, will not be able to make in-game purchases until the platform itself lifts the ban;
— First phase of new anti-bot system has been introduced. It includes a suspicious behavior check mechanism. New features will be added in the following versions.


Improvements


— New mechanical mount, Arantian Rhopard, has been added;
— Mount feed design has been changed due to mechanical mount class introduction.


Fixes


— Issues related to "Aura’s Shield" and "Victim" skills have been fixed;

Huge thanks to all players and External Test Academy alumni helping us improving the game day by day!
